{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788491775,"nonce":"4+HWUM0S8GMoRa8FapT9gaS38Ck=","title":"The chores: what the mod does without a turn","message":"Part of the cockpit round, b4adee2. Design: RUNS/openrun-20260902/audit/COCKPIT.md\n§Chores and §The line.\n\nWHAT\n\nFixed procedures the mod runs when a trigger fires, each with one knob where a\npolicy is involved, each reported in the screen's mod row, none needing a turn.\nThe rule is DESIGN's, ruled on 2026-08-31 and 2026-09-01: where every branch of\nthe response is computable from state the mod already publishes, the mod does\nit, whatever cheaper rung was available. The playbook carries judgement.\n\nThe fact behind it (themes.md T11): the run contract held eleven such rules\nand the agent executed them by hand. Their use decayed by quarter — find-rect\nbefore placing from 22 to 2, saves from 33 to 8, the daily MinifiedThing check\nfrom 3 to 0 — and the quarter with the wipe is the one with the least of it.\nMeat, medicine, cloth and a sculpture deteriorated in storage across four\nslices and no roofing sweep was ever run; the research auto-picker stole hours\nsixteen times in one slice and the agent caught two. A chore has no attention\nbudget.\n\nTHE CHORES\n\nEach becomes its own spec when a worker takes it; two already exist. The\ntrigger, the procedure and the knob are the contract.\n\n1. After a fight — cc8988c, extended. Trigger: standing hostiles reach 0.\n   Rescue downed colonists, nearest capable pawn first; tend each until stable;\n   finish off or capture downed enemies; unforbid what the fight dropped;\n   undraft everyone. Knob: finish off, on only while there is no prison. A\n   colonist downed while hostiles still stand is a decision owed, not a chore —\n   rescue under fire is judgement.\n2. Butcher. Trigger: a fresh corpse of a colony kill or hunt, and a butcher\n   spot or table. Make sure one butcher bill exists and can run (depends on\n   eef837a). No spot: a decision owed carrying the rot deadline. Knob: which\n   animals; default all but pets.\n3. Roof. Trigger: a stored item whose deterioration reasons include being\n   unroofed (Thing.GetInspectStringLowPriority via\n   SteadyEnvironmentEffects.FinalDeteriorationRate — the game's own words).\n   Designate a roof over those cells, as a player would with the roof area\n   tool. Knob: on by default.\n4. Research queue. Trigger: a project finishes and the game auto-picks. Put\n   the next project from the agent's queue back; an empty queue is a decision\n   owed.\n5. A joiner. Trigger: a pawn joins. Essentials to priority 1 — firefighting,\n   patient, basic work, doctor if capable; nothing at 0 unless incapable; the\n   colony's food and outfit policy; the colony's posture. This is 664e9b9's\n   joiner-repair rule, which was structurally inapplicable this run when Tanya\n   joined and died inside a 21-minute window with no agent command. Knob: the\n   essentials list.\n6. A doctor gone — 40ed42f, already specified.\n7. Tend until stable — 7f0e245 comment #2. Trigger: a colonist needs tending\n   and no doctor job starts within a short window. Force the nearest capable\n   pawn, awake or not, and repeat until tending is no longer needed.\n8. Save at every stop — auto-\u003cwhy\u003e-\u003cdate\u003e. Knob: how many to keep. The agent's\n   own `save` stays.\n\nACCEPTANCE\n\n- Each chore has a bench demonstration in which the trigger fires during an\n  advance, the chore completes with no verb from the client, and the next\n  screen's mod row names what it did.\n- A chore that cannot complete produces a decision owed, never a silent skip.\n- The finish-off knob defaults on with no prison and off once one exists, and\n  changing it is a journaled act with a reason.\n- A fresh joiner during an advance: the roster afterwards shows nothing at 0\n  except incapable work types, and the mod row says what was repaired.\n- A raid on a bench with two downed colonists and one downed raider: rescued,\n  tended to stable, raider finished, loot unforbidden, everyone undrafted, with\n  zero client verbs after the raid decision is answered.\n- A fresh corpse left where wildlife will take it, with a butcher spot: a\n  butcher bill runs before the rot deadline; without a spot, the next screen\n  carries the decision with the deadline.","files":null}]}